<title>UK: UKs Major sees inflation falling further.</title>
<headline>UKs Major sees inflation falling further.</headline>
<dateline>PANGBOURNE, England 1997-03-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>Prime Minister John Major said on Wednesday that British inflation would probably fall further and would stay low as long as the government stuck to its current policies.</p>
<p>Major was speaking to pupils at a college in Pangbourne, west of London, during a campaign trip for the May 1 election.</p>
<p>&quot;We have actually got a low inflation economy in this country and it looks as though inflation will go lower still, and if we stick to the broad policies we have followed, it will stay low,&quot; he said.</p>
<p>Britain's current underlying inflation rate is 3.1 percent.</p>
</text>
